  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n80.jpg">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="146" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/1" n="1"/>Halleluyah: Praise the Lord, O my soul, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/2" n="2"/>I shall praise the Lord in my life, I shall sing to the Lord as long as I exist. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/3" n="3"/>Trust not in princes, in the son of man who has no power to help. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/4" n="4"/>When his spirit departs, he returns to his soil, on that day his thoughts perish. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/5" n="5"/>Fortunate is he whose helper is the God of Jacob, whose hope is for the Lord, his God, <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/6" n="6"/>who made heaven and earth, the sea and all that is in it, who keeps faith for ever. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/7" n="7"/>He does justice for <tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n82.jpg" n="26"/>the oppressed and gives bread to the hungry, the Lord frees the fettered. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/8" n="8"/>The Lord makes the blind see, the Lord straightens the bent, the Lord loves the righteous. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/9" n="9"/>The Lord guards strangers, supports the orphan and the widow and the way of the wicked does He pervert. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:rosh_hashanah/morning_psalm_146/10" n="10"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/146/10">The Lord will reign for ever, your God, O Zion, from generation to generation, Halleluyah.</tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
